{"page_content": "COLUMN 1 COLUMN 2 STANDARD SPECIFIC RULES FOR ADAPTATION FROM COLUMN 1 INFORMATION REQUIRED Annexes VII-IX Annex X: 1. Carcinogenicity 1. A carcinogenicity study may be proposed by the registrant or may be study. required by the Agency in accordance with Articles 40 or 41 if: - the substance has a widespread dispersive use or there is evidence of frequent or long-term human exposure; and - the substance is classified as mutagen category 3 or there is evidence from the repeated dose study(ies) that the substance is able to induce hyperplasia and/or pre-neoplastic lesions. If the substance is classified as mutagen category 1 or 2, the default presumption would be that a genotoxic mechanism for carcinogenicity is likely. In these cases, a carcinogenicity test will normally not be required.", "metadata": {"doc_id": "e950d75b-21dc-4d80-bcc7-6e0ec0e81cac", "content_type": "Table", "filename": "information_requirements_r7a_en_part_4.pdf"}}